    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0772" n="758" xml:id="pg758"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> PSA Files: Lot 54D190</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Philippine
                        and Southeast Asian Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lacy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State for Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d487-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-03-13">March 13, 1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I asked Bob Folsom,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d487-f2"/> recently returned from
                    Saigon, to give me his views on the composition of economic missions in
                    Indochina and on Ho Chi Minh. He has embodied those views in the two memoranda
                    which I attach and recommend to your attention.</p>



                <xi:include href="d487-a1.xml" xpointer="d487-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d487-a2.xml" xpointer="d487-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d487-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d487-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted through Deputy Assistant Secretary Merchant.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d487-f2" n="2" xml:id="d487-f2-content">
                <p>Robert S. Folsom, Consul at Saigon since August 1949.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
